# Developer Reference Guide: Core OmniLib House API

This API endpoint reference focuses on executing real-time user-to-user physical asset swaps via the Decentralized Custody Transfer Protocol (DCTP) and managing inter-city cross-routing queries.

## Gateway Security Configuration

All platform integration interactions must pass explicit bearer signature variables inside payload headers.

```http
Authorization: Bearer <YOUR_SECRET_JSON_WEB_TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json
```


## Generate Peer-to-Peer Transfer Token

### Route Definition
`POST /api/v1/assets/exchange/initialize`

Generates a time-locked, signed token enabling an immediate, decentralized physical custody swap between two validated user profiles.

### Request Body Schema

| Variable Name | Type | Obligation | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `asset_id` | `string` | **Required** | The unique internal barcode identifier of the physical book. |
| `current_holder_id` | `string` | **Required** | The account token of the individual relinquishing physical custody. |

#### Example Request Payload
```json
{
  "asset_id": "barcode_99011_omega",
  "current_holder_id": "usr_88219_alpha"
}
```

### Server Response Cycle

#### `201 Created`
The transaction token was successfully registered in the caching layer.

```json
{
  "exchange_token": "DCTP-882-99011-XYZ",
  "time_to_live_seconds": 300,
  "verification_status": "awaiting_receiver_acknowledgment"
}
```

#### `409 Conflict`
Returned if the target asset is already locked by a hold or is marked as missing.

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "ASSET_STATE_LOCKED",
    "message": "This asset is flagged as in-transit and cannot undergo peer exchange verification."
  }
}
```


## Multi-Language Execution Examples

### cURL Execution
```bash
curl -X POST "https://omnilib.house" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer jwt_mock_token_abc" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"asset_id": "barcode_99011_omega", "current_holder_id": "usr_88219_alpha"}'
```

### Python Integration Snippet
```python
import requests

endpoint_gateway = "https://omnilib.house"
connection_headers = {
    "Authorization": "Bearer jwt_mock_token_abc",
    "Content-Type": "application/json"
}
payload_data = {
    "asset_id": "barcode_99011_omega",
    "current_holder_id": "usr_88219_alpha"
}

server_response = requests.post(endpoint_gateway, json=payload_data, headers=connection_headers)
print(f"Status Code: {server_response.status_code}")
```
